   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( y = f(x) \\) be the solution to the differential equation \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = x y \\) with \\( f(2) = 3 \\). Find the approximation to \\( f(1) \\) given by Euler's method, starting at \\( x = 2 \\) with two steps of equal size. Give the exact value."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 0
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The step size is \\( \\Delta x = \\frac{1 - (2)}{2} = - \\frac{1}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( (2, 3) \\) the slope is \\( 6 \\), so \\( y \\approx 3 + (- \\frac{1}{2})(6) = 0 \\) at \\( x = \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (\\frac{3}{2}, 0) \\) the slope is \\( 0 \\), so \\( y \\approx 0 + (- \\frac{1}{2})(0) = 0 \\) at \\( x = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( f(1) \\approx 0 \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      }
